-Brand preparation distinguishes **Core facts prepared** from **Contacts need review**. **Refresh profile** automatically checks the saved website against the company, prepares sourced profile information, then generates the BGP brief. **Refresh BGP take** also prepares any missing prerequisites. Both run in the background and show persistent progress or a specific failure; a blank brief is never reported as refreshed. Clear website matches can be verified from official-site evidence without manual Companies House matching; genuine conflicts still need review. Landlord briefs use their linked properties, deals and relationships. Older retained facts that cannot be corroborated remain flagged and are excluded from a new brief that uses a freshly sourced official profile. Core readiness means official identity and factual profile are prepared; it does not certify every image, company-data source, store, brief or person. Open **Details** for each section's status and the number of automatic sections prepared. Contact review is separate and does not hold up factual preparation.
